{
  "step_by_step_thinking": "The patient is a 28-year-old female with height 179 cm, weight 99 kg, BMI 31 kg/m2, and admission creatinine 1.7 mg/dL. Since BMI is 31 kg/m2, she is obese, so adjusted body weight should be used. Ideal body weight (Devine) for women = 45.5 kg + 2.3 kg per inch over 5 ft. Height = 179 / 2.54 = 70.47 inches; inches over 60 = 10.47. IBW = 45.5 + 2.3 * 10.47 = 69.59 kg. Adjusted body weight = IBW + 0.4 * (actual weight - IBW) = 69.59 + 0.4 * (99 - 69.59) = 81.35 kg. Cockcroft-Gault equation: CrCl = ((140 - age) * weight) / (72 * serum creatinine) * 0.85 for females. CrCl = ((140 - 28) * 81.35) / (72 * 1.7) * 0.85 = 63.3 mL/min.",
  "answer": "63.3 mL/min"
